    },
    {
     "id": "ew",
     "type": "quote",
     "x": 640,
     "y": 230,
     "text": "Wonderful theory,\nwrong species.",
     "by": "E. O. Wilson, on communism",
     "color": "#c792ea",
     "d": 1.8,
     "size": 28,
     "in": 2
    }
   ],
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "In an ant colony, workers share food mouth to mouth, a kind of social stomach. No ant owns anything. The colony is everything."
    },
    {
     "text": "A century ago, the Swiss scientist Auguste Forel held up ants as a model for a cooperative, socialist human society."
    },
    {
     "text": "The biologist E. O. Wilson, who spent his life studying ants, had a sharper line about communism: wonderful theory, wrong species."
    }
   ]
