   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Saad cites research linking higher empathy to stronger support for government redistribution and welfare programs."
    },
    {
     "text": "He also leans on the idea of folk economics. Our intuitions evolved in small bands, where food was shared, and one person's gain often was another's loss."
    },
    {
     "text": "In a modern economy, wealth can grow for everyone, but our instincts still picture a fixed pie."
    }
