   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "He notes that Canada's federal income tax began in 1917, as a temporary wartime measure."
    },
    {
     "text": "And he cites a lab study where people primed to feel empathy became more willing to pay their taxes. For Saad, that's the mechanism: feelings make the bill go down easier."
    },
    {
     "text": "Critics answer that taxes buy roads, schools, courts and safety nets, and that high-tax countries like Denmark consistently rank among the happiest and most prosperous on Earth."
    }
   ]
