   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Next, Canada's public healthcare. Saad stresses that it isn't free. It's paid for through taxes."
    },
    {
     "text": "And waits have grown. A Fraser Institute survey estimated that the median wait from a family doctor's referral to treatment was under ten weeks in 1993, and nearly twenty-eight weeks in 2023."
    },
    {
     "text": "Many Quebecers wait years for a family doctor, and Saad says he pays for private insurance to get timely care."
    }
   ]
