     "d": 1.0,
     "in": 0
    }
   ],
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Finally, he turns to the military, where he argues that recruitment has come to prioritise inclusion over readiness. He cites a reported British Army plan to drop its motto, Be the Best, which in the end it kept."
    },
    {
     "text": "A military's job, he says, is to deter enemies, and empathy is no substitute for strength."
    }
   ]
