   ],
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Critics say Saad underrates what government does well. Public pensions sharply cut poverty among the elderly, and vaccination, clean water and safety rules have saved millions of lives."
    },
    {
     "text": "They also note that markets themselves depend on government: on courts, contracts and property rights."
    },
    {
     "text": "Shared ground: help should be judged by results, not intentions, and every program should be able to answer a simple question. Is this working, and at what cost?"
    }
